WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:38.319
My name is Punmaram and hers is Raeta.

00:00:39.159 --> 00:00:40.360
Wherever I go, she goes.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.919
I look after a herd of 250 camels.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.560
They've always belonged to my family.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.319
My two brothers are coming tomorrow.

00:00:49.759 --> 00:00:52.439
Every year we go to the great
meeting of camel raisers.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.240
It's a long trip on the other side
of the desert South of Rajasthan.

00:00:59.639 --> 00:01:01.599
My oldest brother lives in the village.

00:01:01.919 --> 00:01:02.959
His name is Sutaram.

00:01:03.919 --> 00:01:05.760
He wears the white turban of wisdom.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.879
During the year,
he works the wool of our camels.

00:01:10.599 --> 00:01:13.919
Our tethers, our blankets,
and our rugs are woven from camel hair.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.599
At the great meeting,

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.760
he's the one who speaks for the family.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.720
Sunaram is my little brother.

00:01:31.559 --> 00:01:33.519
He wears the yellow turban of business.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.639
He's always traveling,
looking for new studs.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.879
He's the family business man.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.800
At the great meeting,
he's the one who sells the camels.

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.080
As for me,
I've taken the camel-colored turban

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:50.760
because I'm always with them.

00:01:51.239 --> 00:01:54.120
I guide them from pasture to pasture.

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.400
I saw them all being born.

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.480
They've always seen me here.

00:02:01.839 --> 00:02:04.080
My brothers say that
I'm the father of camels.

00:02:26.839 --> 00:02:27.919
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:45.919
When they're born,

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:49.279
the camels aren't strong enough
to reach their mother's udders.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.199
That's why I'm here,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.199
so that my camels
grow strong and live a long time.

00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:00.639
I belong to the great Rabari tribe.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.880
In Persian, rabar means guide,
but we are not guides for men,

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.759
we are guides for the camels.

00:03:36.279 --> 00:03:40.559
I was 12-years-old when I left my village
to lead this herd with my father.

00:03:41.559 --> 00:03:45.600
Today, it's the biggest one
in Rajasthan with the best camels.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.279
My brothers and I are known for that.

00:03:49.399 --> 00:03:52.919
Every year, to prove that our camels
are the strongest and the fastest,

00:03:53.639 --> 00:03:57.479
one of the three of us goes to the meeting
by crossing the great desert alone.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.559
He rides his favorite camel.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.279
However, for years now,

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.759
I've been the one
to cross the desert with Raeta.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:27.839
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.559
My brothers are leaving
tomorrow for the great meeting.

00:04:56.359 --> 00:04:58.760
They'll take the road
that goes round the desert.

00:04:59.559 --> 00:05:03.720
I'll go across it, right across
the sand where there is no road.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.679
While I'm away, my herd stays here.

00:05:09.239 --> 00:05:11.079
It won't move because of the newborn.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.720
I've had 60 this year
and there are more to come.

00:05:16.519 --> 00:05:20.320
This one's for pretty soon,
but I know she'll wait for me to get back.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.799
They always wait for me to get back.

00:05:24.279 --> 00:05:27.200
There's nothing but females
in my herd and a single male.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.079
I can't keep the young males.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.880
As soon as there are two,
they start to fight.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.519
I've got 40 this year,
they'll be going with my brothers.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.200
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.679
We'll be at the meeting at the full moon.

00:06:10.559 --> 00:06:11.640
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.440
This year,
my brothers don't want me to do it.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.119
They say I'm too old to cross the sand.

00:06:25.359 --> 00:06:26.959
However, I'm going to go anyway.

00:06:31.519 --> 00:06:32.880
Raeta is my best camel.

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:34.279
She will guide me.

00:06:45.559 --> 00:06:46.640
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:08:06.399 --> 00:08:09.119
Jaisalmer, the gateway to the desert.

00:08:13.799 --> 00:08:16.279
Beyond its walls, the tale begins.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:18.279
The land of sand.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.480
No more water.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.520
The man who doesn't forget
lives in the citadel.

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.719
All the camel herders
come to listen to him.

00:08:52.599 --> 00:08:54.200
He tells the story of our tribe.

00:09:03.599 --> 00:09:06.359
In the beginning,
the God Shiva created the first camel,

00:09:07.039 --> 00:09:09.400
and then he created
the first man of my tribe

00:09:09.479 --> 00:09:10.840
to take care of this camel.

00:09:11.799 --> 00:09:13.400
The first camel had five legs.

00:09:14.239 --> 00:09:16.159
Seeing that, the first man asked,

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.320
how the camel
could walk with a leg under its belly.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.200
Shiva took the fifth leg in his hand
and shoved it into the air.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.479
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.559
That's why the camel has a hump.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.799
He said that we were there
to take care of this camel.

00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:36.960
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.559
In the desert,
there are no differences between men.

00:10:20.799 --> 00:10:23.559
In the desert, it's the camel
that makes the difference.

00:10:25.039 --> 00:10:27.599
Raeta will carry me
across the dunes for seven days.

00:10:29.599 --> 00:10:33.440
If our way is straight,
we'll find the city of the Desert Queen.

00:10:34.479 --> 00:10:36.799
Behind her, the great meeting.

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:52.640
My brothers also have a long road,

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:56.400
and the young camels
they've taken with them are still wild.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.440
They've never been tied up.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.640
They've never left their mothers.

00:11:16.799 --> 00:11:17.880
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.880
Here, everything moves.

00:12:40.119 --> 00:12:43.799
From one day to the next, you no
longer recognize the face of the desert.

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:58.239
That's how the Rabari
became nomads, by following the winds,

00:12:58.919 --> 00:13:04.640
the dunes, the rains
and the grazing land to feed their camels.

00:13:07.159 --> 00:13:10.000
My brothers will be worried
if they get there before I do.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.599
They'll blame themselves
for having let me leave.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.159
Out there where so many men
have lost their way.

00:13:22.799 --> 00:13:24.039
However, Reita is strong.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:29.239
She can go five days without water,
if the wind stops blowing.

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:34.840
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:14:39.559 --> 00:14:40.440
The great beauty.

00:14:41.359 --> 00:14:43.880
All tribes gather
at the first moon in April.

00:14:50.960 --> 00:14:54.799
The leaders gather,
listen to complaints, mete out justice

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:56.479
and divide up their territories.

00:14:58.159 --> 00:15:01.039
The families marry off children
and their best animals too.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:05.239
The stories that are told here,
quickly become legends.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.880
Tribes have been coming here
for centuries.

00:15:21.679 --> 00:15:25.159
It's the only place
that has enough water for 100,000 animals.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.440
A great river runs under the sand.

00:15:29.559 --> 00:15:30.719
It has never dried up.

00:15:42.039 --> 00:15:43.119
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:16:07.799 --> 00:16:11.520
There are caravaners, shepherds,
merchants, every race of cattle,

00:16:11.599 --> 00:16:14.200
and all the families
that live from cattle raising.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.679
Each tribe has its own reputation.

00:16:17.919 --> 00:16:21.520
Anything to do with the camels,
it's our family that people come to see.

00:16:22.359 --> 00:16:24.440
It's my elder brother
who does the talking.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.000
However, he won't say anything.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:29.520
Not until the three of us
are there together again

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:31.559
and everybody knows that.

00:16:46.719 --> 00:16:47.799
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:17:04.599 --> 00:17:07.000
My brothers are ripe, I'm getting old.

00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:12.119
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:20.160
The day a camel gives birth,
she only has eyes for her baby.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.479
She can't lead a herd anymore.

00:17:26.479 --> 00:17:28.800
She loses her flexibility
and her faithfulness.

00:17:30.479 --> 00:17:32.520
That's why Raeta hasn't had any children.

00:17:33.439 --> 00:17:34.920
I've needed her too much.

00:17:35.040 --> 00:17:36.119
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:42.439
She'll have one next year
and she'll bring it up.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:45.119
This is our last trip.

00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.760
I was a child when my father
took me off to live with his herd.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:05.640
At first, I was lost in the middle
of all those camels.

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:10.479
I had to get used to drinking
murky water and sleeping out in the cold.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.680
Then my father taught me
to recognize and count them

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:25.199
at a single glance
and how to talk to them from the throat.

00:18:26.719 --> 00:18:30.079
One day he said to me,
man lives on the ground.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:33.800
When he climbs onto a camel, he takes off.

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.479
The city of the Desert Queen.

00:18:48.239 --> 00:18:49.319
The trail ends here.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.800
It is said that the plague
grew in these walls.

00:18:53.599 --> 00:18:55.040
The citizens blamed the rats.

00:18:56.119 --> 00:18:57.079
Then a woman came.

00:18:57.959 --> 00:19:00.959
She gathered the dead children
and changed them into rats

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:02.920
in order to bring them back to life.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:08.319
She said they would be her children
and that all life must be respected,

00:19:09.199 --> 00:19:10.160
even a rat's life.

00:19:11.359 --> 00:19:14.800
The epidemic ended and to thank her,
the people built her a temple

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:19.760
For our family,
she became the goddess of the desert,

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:23.160
the goddess that protects
children from disease.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:27.160
She said that all men
and animals are her children.

00:19:29.959 --> 00:19:31.400
She watches over my camels.

00:21:07.920 --> 00:21:09.000
[Foreign spoken audio]

00:22:25.760 --> 00:22:28.400
Men think that
the solitude of the desert is terrible.

00:22:29.040 --> 00:22:30.640
For me, solitude is here.

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:33.119
I have no life without my herd.

00:23:10.479 --> 00:23:11.319
They're all here.

00:23:24.719 --> 00:23:27.079
My brothers say
I should go back to the village.

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:30.520
That I will have to stop
following the camels one day.

00:25:02.359 --> 00:25:05.000
As long as I'm strong enough
to help a camel be born,

00:25:06.920 --> 00:25:07.959
I'll stay where I am.

